From: Wiam Khader <Wiam@wiamox.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uts: report WiamOX as the system name (uname -s)

UTS_SYSNAME is what uname() returns as sysname. Accepted cost (see
CLAUDE.md, Decisions): autotools config.guess and code that checks
uname -s / platform.system() == "Linux" take their non-Linux path.
/proc/version still starts with "Linux version" (init/version-timestamp.c).

Made against linux 7.3 (kernel.org tarball).
---
--- a/include/linux/uts.h
+++ b/include/linux/uts.h
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
  * Defines for what uname() should return 
  */
 #ifndef UTS_SYSNAME
-#define UTS_SYSNAME "Linux"
+#define UTS_SYSNAME "WiamOX"
 #endif
 
 #ifndef UTS_NODENAME
